## Project Title
Big Cross-Modal Attenuation Correction (BIC-MAC) Challenge
## Overview
About half of the radiation dose of a PET scan is due to the need for a CT scan to quantify produce an attenuation map. Ideally, we would synthesize a CT scan from other data sources (e.g. MRI, X-ray guidance, non-attenutation corrected PET image), so that it can be used for accurate PET image reconstruction.
BIC-MAC is a MICCAI challenge on this topic, with data and evaluation code provided. This hackathon would be a good opportunity to explore the topic further and attempt a submission. See https://bic-mac-challenge.github.io/ for details.
No knowledge of PET or image reconstruction required; this is an image-to-image prediction task.
## Data
Multi-modal data is provided in the challenge. We are allowed to use additional data where it is publicly available.
 
